        The strategic context begins with a limitation: a promise built around
        speed — the 10-minute delivery claim — can only describe a functional
        benefit. As quick commerce normalises across Indian cities, delivery
        windows shrink from a differentiator into a table stake.
      </p>

      <p>
        The opportunity is to look beyond the functional promise and ask a more
        human question: what does convenience genuinely mean in the rhythm of
        an urban life? Moving the brand from being the fastest way to get
        something, to being the least trouble way to live the day.
      </p>

      <div class="case-highlight">
        Speed answers "how fast." Convenience answers "how easy."
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section">
