      <h2>
        The category had already moved beyond emergency shopping.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The research foundation starts from the observation that rapid-delivery
        platforms were initially framed around emergencies — running out of
        something at the wrong moment. In practice, category behaviour has
        moved toward the everyday: small replenishments, missing ingredients, a
        single item that never seemed worth a full trip.
      </p>

